NOTICE
======

This project was not written from scratch. It is derived from Texas
Instruments' Edge AI GStreamer apps and contains third-party components.


Sources it derives from
-----------------------

1. TexasInstruments/edgeai-gst-apps
   https://github.com/TexasInstruments/edgeai-gst-apps

   This forms the basis of the repository. Most of the code under apps_python/,
   configs/, scripts/ and docker/ comes directly from there. The GStreamer
   pipeline setup, config parsing, the pre/post-processing framework and the
   model zoo integration belong to TI.

2. TexasInstruments-Sandbox/edgeai-gst-apps-people-tracking
   https://github.com/TexasInstruments-Sandbox/edgeai-gst-apps-people-tracking

   The Norfair-based object tracking logic comes from there. apps_python/
   path_draw.py comes from that repository; the tracking core of the
   PostProcessTracking class in post_process.py (the Norfair Tracker settings
   and the conversion of detections into Norfair Detection objects) is based on
   the implementation in that repository.

Both repositories are copyright Texas Instruments Incorporated.


Changes made in this repository
-------------------------------

- The dashboard layer (dashboard.py, lite_plot.py, heat_map.py,
  object_time_count.py) was removed entirely; the matplotlib dependency is gone.
- The upstream apps_cpp/ (C++ applications), optiflow/ and tests/ trees were
  removed; this project only uses the Python side and had no dependency on
  those trees. If you need them, take them from the upstream repository above.
  scripts/compile_cpp_apps.sh and the setup_script.sh step that called it were
  removed for the same reason.
- Bounding box drawing with an identity label was added for every tracked
  object.
- Coordinate output normalized against the frame center (dx/dy) and terminal
  reporting were added (PostProcessTracking.tracked_positions).
- The config path in gst_element_map.py was made relative.
- Configuration for the T3 Gemstone O1 / AM67A board and the IMX219 camera was
  added.


